    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30294" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκλάω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνικλάω</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέκλασα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thwart, frustrate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοι ἔωθεν ἐνικλᾶν ὅττικεν εἴπω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.408
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦε τίς ἄτη σωομένους . .
				ἐνέκλασεν</span>; <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.307
			</span></i>; later lit., <i>break in</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιλφίον ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.133
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνὴ ἐγκεκλασμένη</span>
			<i>weak</i> voice, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.80
			</span></i> K. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be bent, inclined</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				<u>Poliorc.</u>
				187.16
			</span></i>; of the eyes of swine, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.671a
			</span></i> (s. v.l.); of a diadem, <i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				8.1
			</span></i>.</div>
